1. Free use for individuals
Any individual may use, copy, study, modify and share Morph Map free of charge for personal, educational, learning, research and non-commercial purposes, provided this licence notice is kept with every copy.

2. Free use for open-source projects
Any public open-source project may use Morph Map free of charge, provided the project is publicly available under an open-source licence and credits Morph Map by name.

3. Paid licence for companies and commercial use
Any company, organisation, agency or other commercial user (including use by employees to do paid work, use inside a business, or use in a product or service sold to others) needs a paid commercial licence from the copyright holder. Until a commercial licence is obtained, such use is not permitted.

4. Citation
Use in a video, course, article, talk or research should credit Morph Map. The repository's Cite this repository citation may be used.

5. No warranty
The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The copyright holder is not liable for any claim, damage or loss arising from its use. Security or accuracy findings are a reading aid, not professional advice.

6. Termination
Rights under this licence end automatically if its terms are breached.

To request a commercial licence, contact the copyright holder through the repository.

Note: this is a plain-language draft. Have a qualified lawyer review it before relying on it for paid licensing.
